<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 16 September, from 681 to 1982.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">681 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,345 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Third Council of Constantinople condemns Pope Honorius I as a heretic</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In its seventeenth session, the Third Council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> decreed that the late Pope <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honorius">Honorius</a> I had spread the heresy of the one will, monothelitism. The council condemned monothelitism and defined Christ as having two wills.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monothelitism">Monothelitism</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1400">1400 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">626 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Owain Glyndŵr is proclaimed Prince of Wales</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Supporters at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glyndyfrdwy">Glyndyfrdwy</a> proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/owain-glyndwr">Owain Glyndŵr</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a>, launching a revolt against English rule. For several years he controlled much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> and summoned Welsh parliaments.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1410">1410 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">616 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The infante Ferdinand takes Antequera from the Emirate of Granada</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a long siege, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antequera">Antequera</a>, a frontier stronghold of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, capitulated to a Castilian army led by the infante Ferdinand of Trastámara. He was known thereafter as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-aragon">Ferdinand of Antequera</a>, and later became Ferdinand I of Aragon.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-aragon">Ferdinand I of Aragon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antequera">Antequera</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1620">1620 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">406 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Mayflower sails from Plymouth</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayflower">Mayflower</a> left Plymouth with 102 passengers, Separatist 'Pilgrims' and others (6 September Old Style). After a gruelling crossing they founded Plymouth Colony in Massachusetts.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">American troops defeat the British at the Battle of Harlem Heights</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a> campaign, just under 1,800 American troops under General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a> defeated just under 1,600 British troops under Brigadier-general Alexander Leslie on Harlem Heights, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan">Manhattan</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan">Manhattan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1810">1810 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">216 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Miguel Hidalgo's 'Grito de Dolores' launches Mexico's revolt</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Priest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miguel-hidalgo-y-costilla">Miguel Hidalgo</a> rang his church bell in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dolores-hidalgo">Dolores</a> and called his parishioners to rise against Spanish rule. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> celebrates the day as Independence Day, won in 1821.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1908">1908 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">118 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Durant incorporates General Motors</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Buick head William Durant formed General Motors as a holding company, soon adding Oldsmobile, Cadillac and others. GM became for decades the world's largest car maker.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1982">1982 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">44 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Phalangist militia begin the Sabra and Shatila massacre</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lebanese Christian militiamen entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beirut">Beirut</a>'s Sabra and Shatila refugee camps, in an area under Israeli control, and killed hundreds of Palestinian and Lebanese civilians over two days.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beirut">Beirut</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 16 September <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-yuan-of-liang"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-yuan-of-liang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emperor Yuan of Liang</span><span class="tp">508–555</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/walter-devereux-1st-earl-of-essex"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/walter-devereux-1st-earl-of-essex.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Walter Devereux, 1st Earl of Essex</span><span class="tp">1541–1576</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bonar-law"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bonar-law.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bonar Law</span><span class="tp">1858–1923</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/yuan-shikai"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/yuan-shikai.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Yuan Shikai</span><span class="tp">1859–1916</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/karl-donitz"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/karl-donitz.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Karl Dönitz</span><span class="tp">1891–1980</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lee-kuan-yew"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lee-kuan-yew.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lee Kuan Yew</span><span class="tp">1923–2015</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jamshid-bin-abdullah"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jamshid-bin-abdullah.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jamshid bin Abdullah</span><span class="tp">b. 1929</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 16 September <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/philip-iii-of-navarre"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/philip-iii-of-navarre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Philip III of Navarre</span><span class="tp">1306–1343</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/catherine-jagiellon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/catherine-jagiellon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Catherine Jagiellon</span><span class="tp">1526–1583</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/quang-trung"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Quang Trung</span><span class="tp">1753–1792</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-xviii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-xviii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis XVIII</span><span class="tp">1755–1824</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edward-whymper"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/edward-whymper.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Edward Whymper</span><span class="tp">1840–1911</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/omar-al-mukhtar"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/omar-al-mukhtar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Omar al-Mukhtar</span><span class="tp">1858–1931</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/christopher-soames"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/christopher-soames.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Christopher Soames</span><span class="tp">1920–1987</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
